From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: gua: adapt platform remove callback to Linux 6.18

Linux 6.18 defines platform_driver.remove as a void callback.  The GUA
IPC wrapper still uses the older int-returning signature, which fails the
build with -Werror=incompatible-pointer-types when HOBOT_REMOTEPROC selects
SND_SOC_GUA.

The callback has no error path, so change it to void and drop the constant
return value.
---
 sound/soc/gua/ipc_wrapper.c | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/gua/ipc_wrapper.c b/sound/soc/gua/ipc_wrapper.c
index 8d07db40d..2b1a0b7b7 100644
--- a/sound/soc/gua/ipc_wrapper.c
+++ b/sound/soc/gua/ipc_wrapper.c
@@ -491,7 +491,7 @@ static int ipc_wrapper_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-static int ipc_wrapper_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
+static void ipc_wrapper_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	ipc_wrapper_data_t *data = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	flush_workqueue(data->hbipc_wq);
@@ -502,8 +502,6 @@ static int ipc_wrapper_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	free_iwrap_sysfs();
 
 	dev_info(&pdev->dev, "AUDIO : audio wrapper remove exit.\n");
-
-	return 0;
 }
 
 static const struct of_device_id ipc_wrapper_dt_ids[] = {
-- 
2.51.0
